    "title": "Coachella YouTube set times revealed: Everything to know for Couchella",
    "text": "April 10, 2026, 12:01 a.m. ETCoachella is here, which means for everyone who can't make it out to the Southern California desert this weekend, Couchella is just a livestream away.The festival will stream for free on YouTube at youtube.com/coachella. It will unfold on seven different channels, each focusing on a different stage, with three channels — Coachella Stage, Outdoor Theatre and Sahara — streaming in 4K.Festival producers have unveiled the set times for this weekend's streams, which include weekend headliners Sabrina Carpenter, Justin Bieber and Karol G.The livestream kicks off at 7 p.m. eastern time on Friday. Set times are below; all times are Eastern Daylight Time.FridayCoachella Stage8:30-9:20 p.m.: Teddy Swims10-10:55 p.m.: The xx12:05-1:35 a.m.: Sabrina Carpenter3-4 a.m.: Anyma presents ÆDENOutdoor Theatre7-7:50 p.m.: Dabeull8:20-9:10 p.m.: Lykke Li9:40-10:30 p.m.: Dijon11:05-12 a.m.: Turnstile1:35-2:50 a.m.: Disclosure2:55-3:55 a.m.: Bonus Set from Do LaBSahara7-7:50 p.m.: Youna7:50-8:50 p.m.: HUGEL9:15-10:15 p.m.: Marlon Hoffstadt11-11:45 p.m.: KATSEYE12:15-1:20 a.m.: Levity1:50-2:40 a.m.: Swae Lee3:05-3:55 a.m.: Sexyy RedMojave7:15-8 p.m.: BINI8:30-9:15 p.m.: Central Cee9:45-10:40 p.m.: Devo11:10-12 a.m.: Moby12:20-1:05 a.m.: Slayyter1:35-2:25 a.m.: Ethel Cain2:55-3:45 a.m.: Blood OrangeGobi7-7:40 p.m.: Bob Baker Marionettes7:45-8:25 p.m.: New Dad8:30-9:10 p.m.: Joyce Manor9:15-9:55 p.m.: CMAT10:20-11 p.m.: fakemink11:25-12:10 a.m.: Holly Humberstone12:50-1:35 p.m.: Joost2:05-2:55 a.m.: Creepy NutsSonora7-7:40 p.m.: Wednesday7:50-8:30 p.m.: Fleshwater9-9:40 p.m.: The Two Lips10:10-11 p.m.: Ninajirachi11:25-12:05 a.m.: Cachirula & Loojan12:15-12:45 p.m.: February1-1:45 a.m.: Hot Mulligan1:55-2:35 a.m.: Carolina Durante2:50-3:50 a.m.: Not for RadioQuasar8-10 p.m.: Tiga10-12 a.m.: Deep Dish12-2 a.m.: PAWSA2-4 a.m.: Disco LinesSaturdayCoachella Stage8:30-9:20 p.m.: Addison Rae10-10:50 p.m.: GIVĒON12-1:10 a.m.: The Strokes2:25-3:55 a.m.: Jus